    "title": "Why is Memorial Day always in May? What’s closed on spring holiday",
    "text": "April 20, 2026, 9:07 a.m. ETMemorial Day — the unofficial start of summer — is the first federal holiday of spring (Juneteenth National Independence Day follows in June), but roughly half of all people don't know what Memorial Day is nor when it occurs, according to Talker Research.Here's when Memorial Day 2026 actually is, and why Memorial Day always falls in May.When is Memorial Day this year?Memorial Day is Monday, May 25, giving mostly all workers and students a three-day weekend.Memorial Day weekend is one of five such three-day holiday weekends this year, joining Martin Luther King Jr. Day, Washington's Birthday, Labor Day and Columbus Day.What is Memorial Day?Memorial Day is federally reserved for honoring the sacrifices of U.S military members that died either in combat or later from wounds suffered in conflicts.\"Memorial Day, a federal holiday held the last Monday in May, is the nation's foremost annual day to mourn and honor its deceased service men and women,\" read the U.S. Department of Veteran Affairs website. \"Originally called Decoration Day, it was formalized by a 'Memorial Day Order' issued by Grand Army of the Republic Commander-in-Chief John A. Logan in 1868.\"The modern proclamation calls on Americans 'to observe Memorial Day by praying, according to their individual religious faith, for permanent peace.'\"Why is Memorial Day always in May?Military.com confirmed Memorial Day emerged from Decoration Day observances while providing additional context.\"In 1971, Congress formalized the timing by designating Memorial Day as the last Monday in May under the Uniform Monday Holiday Act, preserving its historical springtime roots while creating a consistent long weekend,\" read Military.com's website. \"The month thus reflects both the season of remembrance that inspired the holiday and its modern place on the federal calendar.\"Banks, courts will be closed on Memorial DayMajor banks have varying hours for Memorial Day 2026.Bank of America: closedCapital One: closedJPMorgan Chase: closedPNC: closedTD Bank: openTruist: closedWells Fargo: closedAs a federal holiday, most federal and state courts will be closed May 25, but you should check on the status of your specific court matter beforehand.Will mail be delivered on Memorial Day?FedEx locations will be closed on Memorial Day, and the United States Postal Service will not deliver mail on May 25.UPS will also be closed on Memorial Day, and will not process or deliver any packages.Damon C. Williams is a Philadelphia-based journalist reporting on trending, breaking and service-related topics across the Mid-Atlantic region for the USA Today Network.",
